WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
Pablo writes about his future:
Cuando sea mayor, seré médico.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.050
It means "When I'm
older, I'll be a doctor.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.810
" But "I am" is soy.

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.910
So where did this word come from: sea?

5
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.410
Later, he texts his
friend: Quiero que vengas.

6
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.480
That means "I want you to come.

7
00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.630
" You'd expect the normal
form for "you come": vienes.

8
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.910
So why do both swap in
a form you've never met?

9
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.990
In this mission, you'll meet
the present subjunctive: a mood,

10
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.930
not a tense.

11
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.590
You'll learn its singular
forms for five common verbs,

12
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.050
the opposite vowel trick,

13
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.630
and the four situations
that trigger it.

14
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.970
Your mission: find out what
makes Spanish reach for this

15
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.500
mystery form.
